{
  "file": "crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/project_sources.rs",
  "item": "mod[tests]/impl[Project/Domain]/fn[node_path]",
  "citations": [
    {
      "role": "cite",
      "name": "habeas:coverage",
      "commentary": "Source-tool tests publish OutlineData addresses and retain mapped NodeIds\n directly in dependencies. This required Domain method is unused in\n those flows; stable-path and filesystem-storage tests use other domains."
    }
  ],
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The `habeas:coverage` citation on `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/project_sources.rs` `mod[tests]/impl[Project/Domain]/fn[node_path]` is on an explicit function with a body. The explanation is in fenced citation commentary, so it counts as a tracked justification. It is also substantive, and the code agrees with it.\n\n- **Where `node_path` is called.** A search of `crates/trust-but-verify/src` found one non-test caller, `graph.rs` `fn[edge_fingerprint]`. `edge_fingerprint` only calls `node_path` for the targets it is given.\n- **Why `Project` never reaches it.** The `Project` fixture's `outgoing_edges` in the same impl always returns an empty Vec, so `edge_fingerprint` has no targets to hash for it. The `Project` fixture's `load_evidence` and `store_evidence` are in-memory overrides that do not use node paths. Its `Dependency` values in the source tests are all `Dependency::Node` entries mapped directly from `NodeId`s.\n- **Other domains.** The other `node_path` implementations belong to separate fixtures (`Memory`, `TestDomain`, `LookupDomain`, `ReviewDomain`, `StoredGraph`). `StoredGraph` is in `tests/support/stored_graph.rs`, which fits the claim that stable-path and filesystem-storage tests use other domains. I did not read those tests in detail.\n\nThe method is a required trait method that these flows never call. That is a specific reason, not just difficulty. The commentary agrees with the current source, and the citation is not redundant with an `{impl}` or `{test}` reference.",
